// The elements a reader of the screen is told: ids in Tab's order (the
// list's own order before its rows), the element each is in, labels (one ending in ":"
// with the box's text after it) (not a field's value), a box with no room not
// told (it keeps no label), and the focus where a program sent it.
// RUN: sh %S/Inputs/headless.sh %t.dir
// RUN: %ent run -I %t.dir %S/Inputs/layout_access.ent \
// RUN:     2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines

// CHECK:      1: 5 in 0 ""
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: 3 in 0 "Method: GET"
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: 4 in 0 "URL"
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: 6 in 0 "Requests"
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: 1 in 6 "row 0"
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: 2 in 6 "row 1"
// CHECK-NEXT: 1: focus 0
// CHECK:      2: focus 2
